// This source code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0
// © ME Institutional — ME Scalp v3.1
//
// ══ WHAT THIS FILE IS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// v3.1 is v3.0 with the three assigned defects fixed, ten further findings from
// an independent audit addressed, and four additions. The engine — an
// efficiency-ratio regime gate, three triggers (MSS / FVG / sweep), a structural
// stop beyond each setup's own invalidation, fixed-ATR targets — is v3.0's.
//
// ══ PROVENANCE OF THE NUMBERS: THERE ARE NONE ═════════════════════════════════
// v3.0's documentation header — the measurement tables and the v2.5 → v3.0
// deletion rationale — is not in this repository copy. It was trimmed at commit
// time for size, not superseded. v3.1 inherits no measured figures and states
// none of its own. Nothing here has been backtested: this file was written in an
// environment with no market data and no backtest harness, so every hit-rate or
// expectancy table you might look for is absent because the only way to supply
// one would have been to invent it.
//
// NOT MEASURED, and not guessed at anywhere below:
//   · signal frequency, on any symbol or timeframe
//   · hit rate, expectancy, drawdown, or any risk-adjusted figure
//   · the effect of any fix below on the recorded outcome mix
//   · how many signals either new filter removes, or whether the removed ones
//     were the losing ones
//   · whether this makes money on XAUUSD at your broker
//
// ══ UNCOMPILED ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// This file has never been through the Pine compiler. It was verified by reading
// only. Paste it into TradingView's editor and compile it before trusting a line
// of it. Every statement below is a claim about intent, not an observation.
//
// ══ v3.0's SIGNAL SET IS NOT PRESERVED ════════════════════════════════════════
// Read this before comparing charts. Fix F1 changes which bars the FVG rule
// enters on — it was entering on the gap's formation bar, not on a retest — so
// the FVG signal population is materially different from v3.0's, at default
// settings, with no input changed. Any figure ever attached to v3.0's FVG rule
// describes the formation-bar entry and does not carry over. It is withdrawn
// here rather than reused. The MSS and sweep rules are untouched.
// The two new filters are OFF by default and change nothing until switched on.
//
// ══ DEFECTS FIXED ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D1  TP3 was evaluated without `and not slHit`, unlike TP1 and TP2, so a bar
//     spanning both stop and TP3 scored as a win — against the file's own rule
//     that the stop is tested first. Now guarded identically. CONSEQUENCE: plans
//     v3.0 recorded as TP3 may now record as SL or BE. The mix gets worse and
//     more nearly true. Bar-resolution accounting is blind inside the bar; this
//     resolves the ambiguity pessimistically on purpose. A plan already at
//     breakeven that spans BE and TP3 in one bar now records BE.
//
// D2  The dashboard printed nWin/(nWin+nLoss). That denominator dropped every
//     TIME exit, so it was a percentage over a subset while labelled "win"; it
//     also counted a breakeven stop-out as a win. Replaced by four mutually
//     exclusive counters — TP3 / BE / SL / TIME — that sum to the number of
//     closed plans, printed with that denominator stated on the row. No single
//     number replaces it, because no single number was honest.
//     WHAT THE COUNTERS ARE NOT: not a backtest. Counted at bar-close resolution
//     over whatever history the chart loaded, reset on reload, with no spread,
//     commission, slippage or partial fill. They do not model scaling out in
//     thirds: a plan is recorded by the furthest level it reached, so this is a
//     reach profile, not an equity curve. Do not sum it into a P&L.
//
// D3  `riskOk`'s lower bound could never be false — the stop construction floors
//     risk at atr*MIN_RISK + pad, above the threshold it tested. Deleted; the
//     remaining test is the maximum-risk cap, which does bind.
//     Reading that dead code surfaced what it should have been checking. The
//     stop is structural and the targets are ATR-fixed, so a target's R is not a
//     constant: it falls as the stop widens. At the cap (4.00 × ATR) a TP3 of
//     2.0 × ATR is 0.50R — a target worth half what the stop risks. v3.1 adds an
//     optional minimum TP3:risk filter, OFF by default, and makes R visible
//     (ADDITION 1) so the case is legible without the filter.
//
// The following were found by an independent read of v3.0 and are numbered as
// that audit numbered them.
//
// F1  HIGH. "FVG retest" fired on the gap's own formation bar. The push and the
//     trigger loop run in the same `if conf` pass, and the push sets
//     gapBullTop := low, so the loop's first test is `low <= low` — always true.
//     `close >= gapBullBot` was true by the formation condition. The loop runs
//     newest-first with `break`, so the just-born gap always won over a genuine
//     older retest. The rule was a breakout-chase entering at the impulse bar's
//     extreme, and it took its invalidation from high[2] — the far side of that
//     impulse — producing an abnormally wide stop. One breakout bar could also
//     satisfy MSS and FVG at once, so the "two independent confirmations" score
//     component was satisfied by one bar counted twice.
//     FIX: a gap must be at least FVG_MIN_AGE bars old to be retested. This is
//     the change that makes the v3.0 FVG numbers non-transferable.
//     NOT MEASURED: how many signals this removes, or how the survivors behave.
//
// F2  MEDIUM-HIGH. The drawn stop line repainted its whole history at breakeven.
//     `lnSl` is one segment; moving to BE set both endpoints, so the red stop
//     jumped to entry across every bar back to the entry bar and the chart then
//     showed price trading through the drawn stop with the plan still open.
//     FIX: the original stop segment is frozen at the TP1 bar and a second,
//     amber segment starts there at entry. The stop is now stepped, and where it
//     actually sat is preserved. The BE label keeps the original stop price in
//     parentheses so that number is not lost from the chart.
//     The evaluation order is unchanged and is correct: slHit is computed
//     against the old stop, then BE is applied, so BE takes effect from the next
//     bar. Only the drawing lied.
//
// F3  MEDIUM. The two `alertcondition` legs were gated on bare buySignal /
//     sellSignal while plotshape and alert() were gated on `not inTrade[1]`, so
//     an alert could tell the user to enter a trade the indicator itself did not
//     take and drew nothing for. FIX: one pair of gates, `firedBuy`/`firedSell`,
//     used by all three paths.
//
// F4  MEDIUM. "TP1 / TP2 reach" divided by trades OPENED, so an open plan sat in
//     the denominator with no chance of having reached anything — the metric
//     moved on entry, the one event carrying no information about reach. FIX:
//     reaches are tallied when a plan closes, over the closed-plan denominator,
//     which is stated on the row.
//
// F5  MEDIUM. A plan cannot close and another open on the same bar (`fired`
//     reads inTrade before the close is applied). That is kept — changing it
//     alters the signal population in a way that cannot be measured here — but
//     the discarded signal used to leave no trace at all. It still does not
//     enter, and it still does not start the cooldown; it is now counted, and
//     the dashboard shows how many signals the one-plan-at-a-time rule has
//     swallowed. Making the policy visible is not the same as endorsing it.
//
// F6  LOW-MED. On a feed with no volume — several XAUUSD spot feeds — relVol is
//     pinned to 1.0, the participation component is permanently 0 and the score
//     is out of 3, while the panel read "of 4" and a required score of 4 could
//     never be met with no indication why. FIX: the dashboard prints the
//     attainable maximum, says "no volume feed", and turns the row amber when
//     the required score exceeds what this feed can produce. The scoring logic
//     is untouched — awarding the point for absent data would be worse.
//
// F7  LOW. The FVG trigger's `close >= gapBullBot` clause was tautological: the
//     mitigation sweep earlier in the same `if conf` pass had already removed
//     every gap failing it, against the same close. Deleted, both sides. The
//     proof is in the comment at the sweep, so a reader can check it. This
//     leaves the FVG rule visibly resting on fewer conditions than it read as
//     having, which is the honest picture.
//
// F8  LOW. bullName/bullInval fall through to "SWEEP"/low when no trigger fired,
//     so the Risk row printed a concrete, green number for a hypothetical sweep
//     entry on every bar. FIX: the Risk and R rows print "—" with no trigger,
//     like the Trigger row above them always did.
//
// F9  LOW. "Keep completed plans on the chart" deleted the old plan when the
//     NEXT one opened, not at completion, so with it off a finished plan stayed
//     on screen indefinitely at the right edge. The behaviour is the useful one
//     — deleting at completion would erase the outcome label with it — so the
//     input is reworded to say what it does rather than the code changed to
//     match a wrong label.
//
// F10 LOW. `BE_AFTER_1 = true` was a compile-time constant guarding an
//     unconditional branch. Constant and branch removed; breakeven after TP1 is
//     stated as unconditional, which is what it was. tp1Bar/tp2Bar are now reset
//     on entry instead of carrying across plans.
//
// ══ ADDITIONS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// A1  R multiples visible, on the dashboard and in the chart labels. This is the
//     fix for the invisible problem D3 found: the user could read "TP3 = 2.0 ×
//     ATR" off the input panel with no way to see that on this bar it is 0.7R.
//     The dashboard shows the live R of TP1/2/3 for a hypothetical entry at the
//     current close, and the frozen R of the open plan. Labels keep every price
//     v3.0 showed and append R beside it — nothing legible was removed to make
//     room. R = (target − entry) / (entry − stop): a definition, not an estimate.
//
// A2  Session filter, input, OFF by default. Gold behaves differently in the
//     Asian session than in London/NY, so a user may want to stand aside outside
//     chosen hours. It gates ENTRIES only — a plan opened in session is managed
//     to its stop, target or time stop wherever that falls, because closing a
//     live plan because the clock rolled over would be worse than the problem.
//     NOT MEASURED: which sessions suit this engine. The default window in the
//     input is a placeholder, not a finding.
//
// A3  Higher-timeframe agreement, input, OFF by default. Non-repainting by
//     construction, which is the only reason it is here:
//       · request.security(..., lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
//       · the expression returns b[1] — the PREVIOUS, closed HTF bar
//     Both, together. lookahead_off alone still lets the in-progress HTF bar
//     leak into history on a realtime chart; the [1] is what makes a replayed
//     bar agree with what was live. The price of that guarantee, stated plainly:
//     the HTF bias is one full higher-timeframe bar stale, always, by design. If
//     that is unacceptable, leave this off rather than remove the offset. If the
//     HTF series is unavailable the filter reads na and passes rather than
//     silently blocking every signal; the dashboard says so when it happens.
//     NOT MEASURED: whether HTF agreement improves anything here.
//
// A4  Alert payloads carry the trigger name, the trigger count, the risk in
//     price and each target's R, so an alert can be acted on or filtered without
//     re-deriving anything. LIMITATION: `alertcondition` messages must be static
//     text in Pine, so only the `alert()` calls carry the detail. Use those.
//
// ══ DELIBERATELY NOT DONE ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// · No new trigger, score component or confluence layer. v3.0's point was
//   deleting two thirds of v2.5; adding logic back with no way to measure it
//   would undo that for nothing.
// · No intrabar resolution (request.security_lower_tf) for the stop-vs-target
//   ambiguity D1 resolves pessimistically. That is the real fix, it is not free
//   at runtime, and it cannot be validated here.
// · Re-arming on a plan's exit bar (F5). It would change the signal population;
//   it is counted and displayed instead of silently changed.
// · No default was changed. Every behavioural difference from v3.0 is a defect
//   fix, and F1 is the one that moves signals.
//
// ══ KNOWN LIMITS CARRIED OVER FROM v3.0 ═══════════════════════════════════════
// · One plan at a time; a signal on a bar where a plan is open is discarded,
//   including the bar the previous plan closes on (F5).
// · Nothing is evaluated on the entry bar (`bar_index > eBar`). Entry is at that
//   bar's close, so there is no exposure left on it to test.
// · Within one bar the order stop → TP1 → TP2 → TP3 → time is an assumption.
//   The real sequence inside the bar is unknown to this script.
// · Signals require barstate.isconfirmed, so nothing appears and then vanishes
//   intrabar — but a signal is only known at the bar's close.
//
//@version=6
indicator("ME Scalp v3.1", shorttitle="ME Scalp v3.1", overlay=true, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_bars_back=500)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// INPUTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var string G_ENG  = "══ Engine ══"
var string G_FILT = "══ Filters (both off by default) ══"
var string G_TRIG = "══ Triggers ══"
var string G_RISK = "══ Risk & Targets ══"
var string G_DISP = "══ Display ══"

i_freq  = input.string("Standard", "Frequency", options=["Selective", "Standard", "High"], group=G_ENG)
i_dir   = input.string("Both", "Direction", options=["Both", "Long only", "Short only"], group=G_ENG)
i_erLen = input.int(30, "Regime Lookback (bars)", minval=5, maxval=100, group=G_ENG)
i_score = input.int(1, "Quality Score Required (of 4 — max 3 on feeds with no volume)", minval=0, maxval=4, group=G_ENG)

// A2 — entries only. The default window is a placeholder, not a recommendation.
i_useSess = input.bool(false, "Restrict entries to a session", group=G_FILT)
i_sess    = input.session("0800-1700", "Session window", group=G_FILT)
i_tz      = input.string("Exchange", "Session timezone", options=["Exchange", "UTC", "America/New_York", "Europe/London", "Asia/Tokyo", "Asia/Shanghai", "Australia/Sydney"], group=G_FILT)

// A3 — non-repainting HTF bias; one HTF bar stale by design.
i_useHtf = input.bool(false, "Require higher-timeframe agreement", group=G_FILT)
i_htfTf  = input.timeframe("60", "Higher timeframe", group=G_FILT)
i_htfLen = input.int(50, "HTF EMA length", minval=2, maxval=400, group=G_FILT)

i_useMss   = input.bool(true, "MSS — break of the last pivot", group=G_TRIG)
i_useFvg   = input.bool(true, "FVG retest (gap must be ≥1 bar old — see F1)", group=G_TRIG)
i_useSweep = input.bool(true, "Liquidity sweep + reclaim", group=G_TRIG)

i_pad      = input.float(0.45, "Stop Clearance Beyond Invalidation (× ATR)", minval=0.0, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group=G_RISK)
i_breakPad = input.float(0.20, "Extra Clearance for MSS Breaks (× ATR)", minval=0.0, maxval=1.5, step=0.05, group=G_RISK)
i_tp1      = input.float(0.8, "TP1 (× ATR)", minval=0.2, maxval=5.0, step=0.1, group=G_RISK)
i_tp2      = input.float(1.4, "TP2 (× ATR)", minval=0.3, maxval=8.0, step=0.1, group=G_RISK)
i_tp3      = input.float(2.0, "TP3 (× ATR)", minval=0.4, maxval=12.0, step=0.1, group=G_RISK)
i_minR     = input.float(0.0, "Minimum TP3 : risk required (0 = off)", minval=0.0, maxval=5.0, step=0.1, group=G_RISK)
i_timeStop = input.int(12, "Time Stop (bars, 0 = off)", minval=0, maxval=200, group=G_RISK)

i_dash = input.bool(true, "Show dashboard", group=G_DISP)
i_font = input.string("Small", "Text Size", options=["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group=G_DISP)
// F9 — reworded to match what the code does: the old plan is cleared when the
// next one opens, not at completion, so the outcome label survives to be read.
i_keep = input.bool(true, "Keep older plans on the chart (off = show only the latest)", group=G_DISP)

fBody = i_font == "Large" ? size.large : i_font == "Normal" ? size.normal : i_font == "Small" ? size.small : size.tiny
fHead = i_font == "Large" ? size.huge : i_font == "Normal" ? size.large : i_font == "Small" ? size.normal : size.small

erMin      = i_freq == "High" ? 0.25 : i_freq == "Standard" ? 0.32 : 0.40
allowLong  = i_dir != "Short only"
allowShort = i_dir != "Long only"

MIN_RISK    = 0.40
MAX_RISK    = 4.00
COOLDOWN    = 3
FVG_MIN_AGE = 1     // F1: a gap can only be RETESTED on a bar after it formed.

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CORE SERIES
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
atr      = ta.atr(14)
range_   = math.max(high - low, 1e-9)
closePos = (close - low) / range_
body     = math.abs(close - open)
conf     = barstate.isconfirmed

// F6: on a feed that never reports volume this latch stays false, relVol is
// pinned to 1.0, and the participation point can never be earned. The logic is
// left alone; the dashboard reports the reduced maximum instead.
var bool volSeen = false
if nz(volume) > 0
    volSeen := true
volAvg = ta.sma(nz(volume[1]), 20)
relVol = volSeen ? nz(volume) / math.max(volAvg, 1e-9) : 1.0

erNet    = math.abs(close - close[i_erLen])
erPath   = math.sum(math.abs(close - close[1]), i_erLen)
effRatio = erPath > 0 ? erNet / erPath : 0.0
legUp    = close > close[i_erLen]
inTrend  = effRatio >= erMin

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// FILTERS — session and higher timeframe. Both gate ENTRIES only.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
sessTz = i_tz == "Exchange" ? syminfo.timezone : i_tz
inSess = not i_useSess or not na(time(timeframe.period, i_sess, sessTz))

// Returns the PREVIOUS closed HTF bar's bias. The [1] here, with lookahead_off
// at the call site, is what makes this non-repainting. Do not remove either.
htfBias() =>
    e = ta.ema(close, i_htfLen)
    b = close > e ? 1.0 : close < e ? -1.0 : 0.0
    b[1]

htfDir    = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, i_htfTf, htfBias(), lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
htfKnown  = not na(htfDir)
// A close exactly on the HTF EMA reads 0.0 and passes BOTH sides — deliberately
// permissive, so a flat higher timeframe abstains rather than blocking.
htfOkBull = not i_useHtf or not htfKnown or htfDir >= 0.0
htfOkBear = not i_useHtf or not htfKnown or htfDir <= 0.0

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// STRUCTURE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, 2, 2)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low, 2, 2)
var float lastPH = na
var float lastPL = na
if not na(ph)
    lastPH := ph
if not na(pl)
    lastPL := pl

sph = ta.pivothigh(high, 5, 5)
spl = ta.pivotlow(low, 5, 5)
var float sweepHi = na
var float sweepLo = na
if not na(sph)
    sweepHi := sph
if not na(spl)
    sweepLo := spl

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// FAIR VALUE GAPS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var array<float> gapBullTop = array.new_float()
var array<float> gapBullBot = array.new_float()
var array<int>   gapBullBar = array.new_int()
var array<float> gapBearTop = array.new_float()
var array<float> gapBearBot = array.new_float()
var array<int>   gapBearBar = array.new_int()

if conf
    if low > high[2] and (low - high[2]) >= atr * 0.10
        array.push(gapBullTop, low)
        array.push(gapBullBot, high[2])
        array.push(gapBullBar, bar_index)
    if high < low[2] and (low[2] - high) >= atr * 0.10
        array.push(gapBearTop, low[2])
        array.push(gapBearBot, high)
        array.push(gapBearBar, bar_index)
    // Mitigation + expiry sweep. F7: this runs before the trigger loop below, on
    // the same bar and the same `close`, and removes every bull gap with
    // close < gapBullBot and every bear gap with close > gapBearTop. So every gap
    // the trigger loop sees already satisfies those two conditions, which is why
    // the trigger no longer re-tests them.
    if array.size(gapBullBar) > 0
        for k = array.size(gapBullBar) - 1 to 0
            if close < array.get(gapBullBot, k) or bar_index - array.get(gapBullBar, k) > 60
                array.remove(gapBullTop, k)
                array.remove(gapBullBot, k)
                array.remove(gapBullBar, k)
    if array.size(gapBearBar) > 0
        for k = array.size(gapBearBar) - 1 to 0
            if close > array.get(gapBearTop, k) or bar_index - array.get(gapBearBar, k) > 60
                array.remove(gapBearTop, k)
                array.remove(gapBearBot, k)
                array.remove(gapBearBar, k)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TRIGGERS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
mssBull = conf and i_useMss and not na(lastPH) and close >= lastPH + atr * 0.08 and close[1] < lastPH
mssBear = conf and i_useMss and not na(lastPL) and close <= lastPL - atr * 0.08 and close[1] > lastPL

// F1: `bar_index - gapBar >= FVG_MIN_AGE` is the whole fix. Without it the gap
// pushed on THIS bar sets gapBullTop := low and the test below reads low <= low,
// which is always true — the rule entered on the impulse bar, not on a retest.
// F7: the `close >= gapBullBot` clause that stood here is gone; see the sweep.
fvgBull = false
float fvgBullInv = na
if conf and i_useFvg and array.size(gapBullBar) > 0
    for k = array.size(gapBullBar) - 1 to 0
        if bar_index - array.get(gapBullBar, k) >= FVG_MIN_AGE and low <= array.get(gapBullTop, k) and closePos >= 0.55
            fvgBull := true
            fvgBullInv := array.get(gapBullBot, k)
            break
fvgBear = false
float fvgBearInv = na
if conf and i_useFvg and array.size(gapBearBar) > 0
    for k = array.size(gapBearBar) - 1 to 0
        if bar_index - array.get(gapBearBar, k) >= FVG_MIN_AGE and high >= array.get(gapBearBot, k) and closePos <= 0.45
            fvgBear := true
            fvgBearInv := array.get(gapBearTop, k)
            break

swBull = conf and i_useSweep and not na(sweepLo) and (sweepLo - low) >= atr * 0.35 and close > sweepLo and closePos >= 0.55
swBear = conf and i_useSweep and not na(sweepHi) and (high - sweepHi) >= atr * 0.35 and close < sweepHi and closePos <= 0.45

nBull = (mssBull ? 1 : 0) + (fvgBull ? 1 : 0) + (swBull ? 1 : 0)
nBear = (mssBear ? 1 : 0) + (fvgBear ? 1 : 0) + (swBear ? 1 : 0)

bullName = mssBull ? "MSS" : fvgBull ? "FVG" : "SWEEP"
bearName = mssBear ? "MSS" : fvgBear ? "FVG" : "SWEEP"
bullInval = mssBull ? (na(lastPL) ? low : lastPL) : fvgBull ? fvgBullInv : low
bearInval = mssBear ? (na(lastPH) ? high : lastPH) : fvgBear ? fvgBearInv : high

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// QUALITY SCORE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
sPart  = relVol >= 1.15 ? 1 : 0
sBody  = body >= atr * 0.45 ? 1 : 0
scoreBull = sPart + sBody + (closePos >= 0.65 ? 1 : 0) + (nBull >= 2 ? 1 : 0)
scoreBear = sPart + sBody + (closePos <= 0.35 ? 1 : 0) + (nBear >= 2 ? 1 : 0)
scoreMax  = volSeen ? 4 : 3     // F6

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// THE STOP, THE TARGETS, AND THE R THAT FALLS OUT OF THEM
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
padBull = atr * (i_pad + (bullName == "MSS" ? i_breakPad : 0.0))
padBear = atr * (i_pad + (bearName == "MSS" ? i_breakPad : 0.0))
// The math.min/max against close ∓ atr*MIN_RISK is the risk FLOOR. Risk can never
// be below atr*MIN_RISK + pad, which is why D3's lower bound was dead code.
slBull  = math.min(bullInval, close - atr * MIN_RISK) - padBull
slBear  = math.max(bearInval, close + atr * MIN_RISK) + padBear
riskBull = close - slBull
riskBear = slBear - close
// D3 — only the cap can bind; the floor is enforced above by construction.
riskCapBull = riskBull <= atr * MAX_RISK
riskCapBear = riskBear <= atr * MAX_RISK

buyTp1  = close + atr * i_tp1
buyTp2  = close + atr * i_tp2
buyTp3  = close + atr * i_tp3
sellTp1 = close - atr * i_tp1
sellTp2 = close - atr * i_tp2
sellTp3 = close - atr * i_tp3

// A1 — R = (target − entry) / (entry − stop). Not a constant: the stop is
// structural and the targets are ATR-fixed, so R falls as the stop widens.
r1Bull = riskBull > 0 ? (buyTp1 - close) / riskBull : 0.0
r2Bull = riskBull > 0 ? (buyTp2 - close) / riskBull : 0.0
r3Bull = riskBull > 0 ? (buyTp3 - close) / riskBull : 0.0
r1Bear = riskBear > 0 ? (close - sellTp1) / riskBear : 0.0
r2Bear = riskBear > 0 ? (close - sellTp2) / riskBear : 0.0
r3Bear = riskBear > 0 ? (close - sellTp3) / riskBear : 0.0

// D3 — the meaningful check that replaces the dead one. Off by default.
minROkBull = i_minR <= 0.0 or r3Bull >= i_minR
minROkBear = i_minR <= 0.0 or r3Bear >= i_minR

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SIGNAL
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int lastSigBar = -100000
coolOk = bar_index - lastSigBar >= COOLDOWN
buySignal  = nBull > 0 and allowLong  and close > open and coolOk and riskCapBull and minROkBull and scoreBull >= i_score and inTrend and legUp and inSess and htfOkBull
sellSignal = nBear > 0 and allowShort and close < open and coolOk and riskCapBear and minROkBear and scoreBear >= i_score and inTrend and not legUp and inSess and htfOkBear

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TRADE STATE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var bool   inTrade  = false
var bool   tradeBuy = false
var float  eEntry   = na
var float  eSl      = na
var float  eSl0     = na    // F2: the stop as first placed, kept after BE.
var float  eT1      = na
var float  eT2      = na
var float  eT3      = na
var float  eRisk    = na
var float  eR1      = na
var float  eR2      = na
var float  eR3      = na
var int    eBar     = na
var bool   eTp1     = false
var bool   eTp2     = false
var string eName    = ""
var int    nTrades  = 0
// F4 — reach counters are tallied at CLOSE, over the closed-plan denominator.
var int    nTp1     = 0
var int    nTp2     = 0
// D2 — mutually exclusive; these four sum to the number of closed plans.
var int    nTp3     = 0
var int    nBE      = 0
var int    nSL      = 0
var int    nTime    = 0
// F5 — signals discarded because a plan was already open. Counted, not taken.
var int    nSupp    = 0
var int    tp1Bar   = na
var int    tp2Bar   = na

// F3 — one pair of gates for plotshape, alert() and alertcondition alike.
// `inTrade` is read here before the block below can change it, so these equal
// v3.0's `not inTrade[1]`.
firedBuy      = buySignal  and not inTrade
firedSell     = sellSignal and not inTrade
fired         = firedBuy or firedSell
suppressedNow = (buySignal or sellSignal) and inTrade
if suppressedNow
    nSupp := nSupp + 1

if fired
    inTrade  := true
    tradeBuy := firedBuy
    eEntry   := close
    eSl      := firedBuy ? slBull : slBear
    eSl0     := eSl
    eT1      := firedBuy ? buyTp1 : sellTp1
    eT2      := firedBuy ? buyTp2 : sellTp2
    eT3      := firedBuy ? buyTp3 : sellTp3
    eRisk    := firedBuy ? riskBull : riskBear
    eR1      := firedBuy ? r1Bull : r1Bear
    eR2      := firedBuy ? r2Bull : r2Bear
    eR3      := firedBuy ? r3Bull : r3Bear
    eBar     := bar_index
    eTp1     := false
    eTp2     := false
    tp1Bar   := na          // F10 — no longer carried across plans.
    tp2Bar   := na
    eName    := firedBuy ? bullName : bearName
    lastSigBar := bar_index
    nTrades  := nTrades + 1

slHit  = false
tpHit  = false
timeUp = false
if inTrade and conf and bar_index > eBar
    // The stop is tested FIRST, and every target below is guarded by it.
    slHit := tradeBuy ? low <= eSl : high >= eSl
    if not eTp1
        bool t1 = tradeBuy ? high >= eT1 : low <= eT1
        if t1 and not slHit
            eTp1   := true
            tp1Bar := bar_index
            // F10 — breakeven after TP1 is unconditional; the constant that
            // guarded this was always true. It takes effect from the NEXT bar,
            // because slHit above was already computed against the old stop.
            eSl := eEntry
    if not eTp2
        bool t2 = tradeBuy ? high >= eT2 : low <= eT2
        if t2 and not slHit
            eTp2   := true
            tp2Bar := bar_index
    // D1 — `and not slHit`, matching TP1 and TP2. A bar spanning both the stop
    // and TP3 now resolves to the stop, not to a win.
    tpHit  := (tradeBuy ? high >= eT3 : low <= eT3) and not slHit
    timeUp := i_timeStop > 0 and (bar_index - eBar) >= i_timeStop

justClosed = inTrade and (slHit or tpHit or timeUp)
legTxt   = eTp2 ? "TP2 ✓ " : eTp1 ? "TP1 ✓ " : ""
// Precedence matches the resolution order above: stop, then target, then time.
closeTxt = slHit ? (eTp1 ? legTxt + "→ BE" : "SL ✕") : tpHit ? "TP3 ✓" : legTxt + "TIME"
closeCol = slHit and eTp1 ? color.new(#FFC400, 0) : slHit ? color.new(#FF1744, 0) : tpHit ? color.new(#00E676, 0) : color.new(#888888, 0)
if justClosed
    if eTp1                     // F4 — tallied here, not while the plan is open.
        nTp1 := nTp1 + 1
    if eTp2
        nTp2 := nTp2 + 1
    if slHit                    // D2 — four exclusive outcomes.
        if eTp1
            nBE := nBE + 1
        else
            nSL := nSL + 1
    else if tpHit
        nTp3 := nTp3 + 1
    else
        nTime := nTime + 1
    inTrade := false

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PLOTTING
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
plotshape(not na(tp1Bar) and tp1Bar == bar_index and tradeBuy,      "TP1 hit (long)",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.new(#00E676, 30), size=size.tiny)
plotshape(not na(tp1Bar) and tp1Bar == bar_index and not tradeBuy,  "TP1 hit (short)", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.new(#00E676, 30), size=size.tiny)
plotshape(not na(tp2Bar) and tp2Bar == bar_index and tradeBuy,      "TP2 hit (long)",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.new(#00E676, 0),  size=size.tiny)
plotshape(not na(tp2Bar) and tp2Bar == bar_index and not tradeBuy,  "TP2 hit (short)", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.new(#00E676, 0),  size=size.tiny)
plotshape(firedBuy,  "BUY",  shape.labelup,   location.belowbar, color.new(#00E676, 0), text="BUY",  textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
plotshape(firedSell, "SELL", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(#FF1744, 0), text="SELL", textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
bgcolor(inTrend ? color.new(legUp ? #00E676 : #FF1744, 94) : na, title="Regime")

var line  lnEn = na
var line  lnSl = na
var line  lnBe = na          // F2 — the stepped breakeven segment.
var line  lnT1 = na
var line  lnT2 = na
var line  lnT3 = na
var label lbEn = na
var label lbSl = na
var label lbT1 = na
var label lbT2 = na
var label lbT3 = na
var label lbEnd = na
var bool  beDrawn = false

// A1 — labels keep every price v3.0 showed and append R beside it.
rTxt(float r) =>
    str.tostring(r, "0.00") + "R"

if fired
    if not na(lnSl) and not i_keep
        line.delete(lnEn)
        line.delete(lnSl)
        line.delete(lnBe)
        line.delete(lnT1)
        line.delete(lnT2)
        line.delete(lnT3)
        label.delete(lbEn)
        label.delete(lbSl)
        label.delete(lbT1)
        label.delete(lbT2)
        label.delete(lbT3)
        label.delete(lbEnd)
    lnBe    := na            // drop the handle so the new plan cannot extend it
    beDrawn := false
    lnEn := line.new(bar_index, eEntry, bar_index, eEntry, color=color.new(#FFFFFF, 25), style=line.style_dotted)
    lnSl := line.new(bar_index, eSl, bar_index, eSl, color=color.new(#FF1744, 0), width=2)
    lnT1 := line.new(bar_index, eT1, bar_index, eT1, color=color.new(#00E676, 20), style=line.style_dashed)
    lnT2 := line.new(bar_index, eT2, bar_index, eT2, color=color.new(#00E676, 40), style=line.style_dashed)
    lnT3 := line.new(bar_index, eT3, bar_index, eT3, color=color.new(#00E676, 60), style=line.style_dashed)
    lbEn := label.new(bar_index, eEntry, "ENTRY " + str.tostring(eEntry, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=color.new(#FFFFFF, 0), size=fBody)
    lbSl := label.new(bar_index, eSl, "SL " + str.tostring(eSl, format.mintick) + "  (1R = " + str.tostring(eRisk, format.mintick) + ")", style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=color.new(#FF1744, 0), size=fBody)
    lbT1 := label.new(bar_index, eT1, "TP1 " + str.tostring(eT1, format.mintick) + "  " + rTxt(eR1), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=color.new(#00E676, 0), size=fBody)
    lbT2 := label.new(bar_index, eT2, "TP2 " + str.tostring(eT2, format.mintick) + "  " + rTxt(eR2), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=color.new(#00E676, 20), size=fBody)
    lbT3 := label.new(bar_index, eT3, "TP3 " + str.tostring(eT3, format.mintick) + "  " + rTxt(eR3), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=color.new(#00E676, 40), size=fBody)

if inTrade and not na(lnSl)
    line.set_x2(lnEn, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT1, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT2, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT3, bar_index)
    // F2 — the stop is STEPPED, never rewritten. The red segment stops at the
    // TP1 bar showing where the stop actually was; an amber segment carries the
    // breakeven level forward from there. Neither endpoint of lnSl is ever moved
    // in price, which is the whole point of the fix.
    if eTp1
        if not beDrawn
            line.set_x2(lnSl, bar_index)
            lnBe := line.new(bar_index, eEntry, bar_index, eEntry, color=color.new(#FFC400, 0), width=2)
            beDrawn := true
        else
            line.set_x2(lnBe, bar_index)
    else
        line.set_x2(lnSl, bar_index)
    label.set_x(lbEn, bar_index)
    label.set_x(lbSl, bar_index)
    label.set_y(lbSl, eSl)
    // The original stop price stays on the chart in parentheses — the BE move
    // must not delete the provenance of the number the plan was sized on.
    label.set_text(lbSl, eTp1 ? "BE " + str.tostring(eSl, format.mintick) + "  (0.00R at risk · orig SL " + str.tostring(eSl0, format.mintick) + ")" : "SL " + str.tostring(eSl, format.mintick) + "  (1R = " + str.tostring(eRisk, format.mintick) + ")")
    label.set_textcolor(lbSl, eTp1 ? color.new(#FFC400, 0) : color.new(#FF1744, 0))
    if eTp1
        label.set_text(lbT1, "TP1 ✓ " + str.tostring(eT1, format.mintick) + "  " + rTxt(eR1))
    if eTp2
        label.set_text(lbT2, "TP2 ✓ " + str.tostring(eT2, format.mintick) + "  " + rTxt(eR2))
    label.set_x(lbT1, bar_index)
    label.set_x(lbT2, bar_index)
    label.set_x(lbT3, bar_index)

if justClosed and not na(lnSl)
    line.set_x2(lnEn, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT1, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT2, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT3, bar_index)
    if beDrawn
        line.set_x2(lnBe, bar_index)
    else
        line.set_x2(lnSl, bar_index)
    lbEnd := label.new(bar_index, tradeBuy ? low : high, closeTxt,
         style=tradeBuy ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
         color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=closeCol, size=fBody)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// DASHBOARD
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
pctTxt(int part, int total) =>
    total > 0 ? str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * part / total)) + "%" : "—"

var table dash = na
if i_dash and barstate.islast
    if na(dash)
        dash := table.new(position.top_right, 3, 13, bgcolor=color.rgb(10, 10, 15, 5), border_width=1, border_color=color.rgb(40, 40, 50))
    grn = color.new(#00E676, 0)
    red = color.new(#FF1744, 0)
    dim = color.new(#888888, 0)
    yel = color.new(#FFC400, 0)
    wht = color.new(#FFFFFF, 0)
    hdr = color.rgb(14, 14, 20)

    nClosed  = nTp3 + nBE + nSL + nTime
    scoreBad = i_score > scoreMax    // F6 — a requirement this feed cannot meet

    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "ME SCALP v3.1 — " + str.upper(i_freq), text_color=wht, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 20), text_size=fHead, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, "", bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 20))
    table.cell(dash, 2, 0, str.tostring(nTrades) + " opened", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 20))

    table.cell(dash, 0, 1, "", text_size=fBody, bgcolor=hdr)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 1, "BUY",  text_color=grn, text_size=fBody, bgcolor=hdr)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 1, "SELL", text_color=red, text_size=fBody, bgcolor=hdr)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 2, "Regime (ER≥" + str.tostring(erMin, "0.00") + ")", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=hdr)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 2, (inTrend ? (legUp ? "TREND ▲" : "TREND ▼") : "CHOP") + "  " + str.tostring(effRatio, "0.00"), text_color=inTrend ? (legUp ? grn : red) : yel, text_size=fBody)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 2, inTrend ? (legUp ? "longs only" : "shorts only") : "standing aside", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 3, "Trigger", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=hdr)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 3, nBull > 0 ? bullName + " ×" + str.tostring(nBull) : "—", text_color=nBull > 0 ? grn : dim, text_size=fBody)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 3, nBear > 0 ? bearName + " ×" + str.tostring(nBear) : "—", text_color=nBear > 0 ? red : dim, text_size=fBody)

    // F6 — the attainable maximum, not a hardcoded 4.
    table.cell(dash, 0, 4, "Score — need " + str.tostring(i_score) + "/" + str.tostring(scoreMax) + (volSeen ? "" : "\nno volume feed: max 3"), text_color=scoreBad ? yel : dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=hdr)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 4, str.tostring(scoreBull) + "/" + str.tostring(scoreMax), text_color=scoreBad ? yel : (scoreBull >= i_score ? grn : dim), text_size=fBody)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 4, str.tostring(scoreBear) + "/" + str.tostring(scoreMax), text_color=scoreBad ? yel : (scoreBear >= i_score ? red : dim), text_size=fBody)

    // F8 — with no trigger, bullName/bullInval fall through to a fabricated
    // sweep entry off this bar's low. Print "—" rather than a number for a setup
    // that does not exist.
    table.cell(dash, 0, 5, "Risk (× ATR, cap " + str.tostring(MAX_RISK, "0.00") + ")", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=hdr)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 5, nBull > 0 ? str.tostring(riskBull / math.max(atr, 1e-9), "0.00") : "—", text_color=nBull > 0 and riskCapBull ? grn : dim, text_size=fBody)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 5, nBear > 0 ? str.tostring(riskBear / math.max(atr, 1e-9), "0.00") : "—", text_color=nBear > 0 and riskCapBear ? red : dim, text_size=fBody)

    // A1 — live R of the three targets, for a hypothetical entry at this close.
    table.cell(dash, 0, 6, "TP1/2/3 in R" + (i_minR > 0 ? "\nneed TP3 ≥ " + str.tostring(i_minR, "0.0") : ""), text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=hdr)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 6, nBull > 0 ? str.tostring(r1Bull, "0.00") + " / " + str.tostring(r2Bull, "0.00") + " / " + str.tostring(r3Bull, "0.00") : "—", text_color=nBull == 0 ? dim : (minROkBull ? grn : yel), text_size=fBody)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 6, nBear > 0 ? str.tostring(r1Bear, "0.00") + " / " + str.tostring(r2Bear, "0.00") + " / " + str.tostring(r3Bear, "0.00") : "—", text_color=nBear == 0 ? dim : (minROkBear ? red : yel), text_size=fBody)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 7, "Filters", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=hdr)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 7, not i_useSess ? "session off" : (inSess ? "in session" : "OUT of session"), text_color=not i_useSess ? dim : (inSess ? grn : yel), text_size=fBody)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 7, not i_useHtf ? "HTF off" : (not htfKnown ? "HTF n/a — passing" : (htfDir > 0 ? i_htfTf + " up (prev bar)" : htfDir < 0 ? i_htfTf + " down (prev bar)" : i_htfTf + " flat")), text_color=not i_useHtf ? dim : (not htfKnown ? yel : (htfDir > 0 ? grn : htfDir < 0 ? red : yel)), text_size=fBody)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 8, "Open plan", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 22))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 8, inTrade ? (tradeBuy ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + eName + "  " + str.tostring(bar_index - eBar) + "b" + (eTp1 ? "  BE" : "") : "flat", text_color=inTrade ? (tradeBuy ? grn : red) : dim, text_size=fBody)
    // F5 — signals the one-plan-at-a-time rule swallowed, made visible.
    table.cell(dash, 2, 8, inTrade and i_timeStop > 0 ? "close in " + str.tostring(math.max(i_timeStop - (bar_index - eBar), 0)) + "b" : (nSupp > 0 ? str.tostring(nSupp) + " signal bars skipped\n(a plan was open)" : ""), text_color=dim, text_size=fBody)

    // A1 — the OPEN plan's R, frozen at its entry. Not the live row above.
    table.cell(dash, 0, 9, "Open plan R", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 22))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 9, inTrade ? str.tostring(eR1, "0.00") + " / " + str.tostring(eR2, "0.00") + " / " + str.tostring(eR3, "0.00") : "—", text_color=inTrade ? wht : dim, text_size=fBody)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 9, inTrade ? "1R = " + str.tostring(eRisk, format.mintick) : "", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody)

    // F4 — numerator and denominator both over CLOSED plans, denominator stated.
    table.cell(dash, 0, 10, "TP1 / TP2 reached", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 22))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 10, nClosed > 0 ? pctTxt(nTp1, nClosed) + " / " + pctTxt(nTp2, nClosed) : "—", text_color=nClosed == 0 ? dim : wht, text_size=fBody)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 10, "of " + str.tostring(nClosed) + " closed", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody)

    // D2 — four exclusive counters summing to nClosed. No single "% win" over a
    // denominator that quietly dropped the TIME exits.
    table.cell(dash, 0, 11, "Outcome mix", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 22))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 11, "TP3 " + str.tostring(nTp3) + "  ·  BE " + str.tostring(nBE), text_color=nClosed == 0 ? dim : grn, text_size=fBody)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 11, "SL " + str.tostring(nSL) + "  ·  TIME " + str.tostring(nTime), text_color=nClosed == 0 ? dim : red, text_size=fBody)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 12, "of " + str.tostring(nClosed) + " closed\nnot a backtest", text_color=dim, text_size=fBody, text_halign=text.align_left, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 22))
    table.cell(dash, 1, 12, pctTxt(nTp3, nClosed) + "  ·  " + pctTxt(nBE, nClosed), text_color=nClosed == 0 ? dim : grn, text_size=fBody)
    table.cell(dash, 2, 12, pctTxt(nSL, nClosed) + "  ·  " + pctTxt(nTime, nClosed), text_color=nClosed == 0 ? dim : red, text_size=fBody)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ALERTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// A4 — trigger name, trigger count, risk in price, and each target's R.
// F3 — gated identically to the chart, so an alert never announces a trade the
// indicator did not take.
if firedBuy
    alert("ME Scalp v3.1 BUY | trigger " + bullName + " ×" + str.tostring(nBull) + " | entry " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + " | SL " + str.tostring(slBull, format.mintick) + " (1R = " + str.tostring(riskBull, format.mintick) + ") | TP1 " + str.tostring(buyTp1, format.mintick) + " " + rTxt(r1Bull) + " | TP2 " + str.tostring(buyTp2, format.mintick) + " " + rTxt(r2Bull) + " | TP3 " + str.tostring(buyTp3, format.mintick) + " " + rTxt(r3Bull), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if firedSell
    alert("ME Scalp v3.1 SELL | trigger " + bearName + " ×" + str.tostring(nBear) + " | entry " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + " | SL " + str.tostring(slBear, format.mintick) + " (1R = " + str.tostring(riskBear, format.mintick) + ") | TP1 " + str.tostring(sellTp1, format.mintick) + " " + rTxt(r1Bear) + " | TP2 " + str.tostring(sellTp2, format.mintick) + " " + rTxt(r2Bear) + " | TP3 " + str.tostring(sellTp3, format.mintick) + " " + rTxt(r3Bear), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// Static text only — Pine does not allow a dynamic message on alertcondition.
// The detail is in the alert() calls above. Gating now matches them (F3).
alertcondition(firedBuy,  "ME Scalp — BUY",  "ME Scalp BUY")
alertcondition(firedSell, "ME Scalp — SELL", "ME Scalp SELL")
